### Interpolate Query Parameters in TypeScript

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/moosestack/apis/analytics-api.mdx

Use template literals with Moose's `sql.statement` to safely interpolate variables into SQL queries. Ensure variables are properly escaped and typed.

```typescript
import { UserTable } from "./UserTable";

const minAge = 18;
const userRole = "admin";

const query = sql.statement`
  SELECT * FROM ${UserTable}
  WHERE age > ${minAge}
  AND role = ${userRole}
`;

// MooseClient handles type conversion and escaping
const data = await client.query.execute<UserSchema>(query);

// EXECUTION: SELECT * FROM users WHERE age > 18 AND role = 'admin'
```

```typescript
import { OlapTable } from "@514labs/moose-lib";

interface UserSchema {
  id: Key<number>
  name: string
  email: string
}

export const UserTable = new OlapTable<UserSchema>("users")
```

