### Define TypeScript Data Model with OlapTable

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/guides/production-ready-analytics-agent/tutorial.mdx

Defines a data model for ClickHouse using `OlapTable`, specifying engine and ordering fields. Also shows how to define a `Stream` for data ingestion and an `IngestApi` for data processing.

```typescript
import { OlapTable, Stream, IngestApi, ClickHouseEngines } from "@514labs/moose-lib";

export const MyTable = new OlapTable<MyData>("my_table", {
  engine: ClickHouseEngines.MergeTree,
  orderByFields: ["low_cardinality_field", "timestamp"],
});

export const MyStream = new Stream<MyData>("my_data", {
  destination: MyTable,
});

export const MyIngestApi = new IngestApi<MyData>("my_data", {
  destination: MyStream,
});
```

